# Who must review a change to the harness. HARNESS.md names the owner: Alex Morgan (@alex-morgan), with the
# course's teaching assistants (@studybuddy/tas) as the second pair of eyes.
# Lines work like .gitignore, and the LAST matching line wins: broad lines first, the strict ones after them.

# The harness: what the agent loads, how it is guarded and measured, and how it is released.
/AGENTS.md              @alex-morgan @studybuddy/tas
**/AGENTS.md            @alex-morgan @studybuddy/tas
*.instructions.md       @alex-morgan @studybuddy/tas
/HARNESS.md             @alex-morgan @studybuddy/tas
/.github/               @alex-morgan @studybuddy/tas
/.mcp.json              @alex-morgan @studybuddy/tas
/mcp/                   @alex-morgan @studybuddy/tas
/apm.yml                @alex-morgan @studybuddy/tas
/apm.lock.yaml          @alex-morgan @studybuddy/tas
/scripts/               @alex-morgan @studybuddy/tas
/evals/                 @alex-morgan @studybuddy/tas
/attacks/               @alex-morgan @studybuddy/tas
/attacks.local.json     @alex-morgan @studybuddy/tas
/CHANGELOG.md           @alex-morgan @studybuddy/tas
/dist/                  @alex-morgan

# The controls themselves: only the owner. GitHub accepts a review from any one of a line's owners, so these lines
# name only Alex: a change here can weaken or switch off the other checks (the hooks, the gate's workflows, the
# scripts whose exit code is the gate, the eval baseline and comparison, the shipped attack pack, this file).
/harness.json               @alex-morgan
/.github/hooks/             @alex-morgan
/.github/workflows/         @alex-morgan
/.github/CODEOWNERS         @alex-morgan
/scripts/harness-check.mjs  @alex-morgan
/scripts/attack.mjs         @alex-morgan
/scripts/eval.mjs           @alex-morgan
/scripts/eval/              @alex-morgan
/evals/baseline.json        @alex-morgan
/attacks/pack.json          @alex-morgan
